1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,103
Someone faints?

2
00:00:01,103 --> 00:00:02,127
Here's what to do.

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,948
1 — Check they respond and are breathing.

4
00:00:07,948 --> 00:00:10,038
Call their name and tap their shoulder.

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:16,199
2 — Lay them flat on their back and raise their legs about 30 centimetres, or one foot.

6
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:20,181
3 — Loosen tight clothing, give fresh air and stay with them.

7
00:00:20,181 --> 00:00:21,956
They should wake within a minute.

8
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,969
When they wake, let them sit up slowly.

9
00:00:24,969 --> 00:00:27,396
Give water or food only once fully alert.

10
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:31,424
Don't sit them up fast, slap them or leave them alone.

11
00:00:31,424 --> 00:00:34,325
Never give food or drink to someone unconscious.

12
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:41,025
Call emergency services if they don't wake within a minute, aren't breathing, are hurt, or have chest pain.

13
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:46,435
See a doctor after a first faint, repeated faints, pregnancy or heart problems.
